            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Donna Aki"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved this recipe. I used all purpose flour instead of the rice and tapioca flours and it turned out beautifully. I lined the bottom of a spring form pan with banana leaves, put half the batter in, layered the coconut flakes/salt mixture then the rest of the batter. Topped with banana leaves for that wonderful flavour. YUM",
            "datePublished": "2021-07-25T20:21:28.967Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Irene Y"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tasty. I didn't have arrowroot starch, but used potato starch as I think they should be similar. My bananas were extremely ripe, so I did not add any sugar at all. It was sweet enough for me. As a preference I just sprinkled a bit of coconut on top instead of measuring it out. I made this in silicone muffin cups, but might try making this again with banana leaves.",
            "datePublished": "2018-04-09T23:38:58.443Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AKeenCook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I prepared it for my family and they all gave it a thumbs up! This cake has a dense texture that is commonly found in southeast asian cakes, which I found to be quite nice. You can taste the banana and coconut with every bite you take! Thumbs up for the creator of this dish, will make again.",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-15T09:21:10.780Z"
          }
